error[E0277]: `Cons<A, Cons<B, notko_hlist::Empty>>` does not hold `Absent`
  --> tests/compile_fail/an_absent_type_is_not_held.rs:16:13
   |
16 |     holds::<Two, Absent>();
   |             ^^^ the trait `Contains<Absent>` is not implemented for `Cons<A, Cons<B, notko_hlist::Empty>>`
   |
   = note: Membership is decided by walking the cells, so `Cons<A, Cons<B, notko_hlist::Empty>>` has to be a list built from `Empty` and `Cons<H, T>`, and `Absent` has to be one of its heads. If the compiler reports `overflow evaluating the requirement` instead, the list is deeper than the default recursion limit and the crate root wants `#![recursion_limit = "1024"]`.
note: required by a bound in `holds`
  --> tests/compile_fail/an_absent_type_is_not_held.rs:13:13
   |
13 | fn holds<L: Contains<X>, X>() {}
   |             ^^^^^^^^^^^ required by this bound in `holds`
